            <!-- Daemon Mode -->
            <div slot="doc-14">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gar-text-primary mb-4">Daemon Mode</h3>
              <p class="text-gar-text-secondary mb-4">
                In daemon mode, garlaunch listens for IPC commands and spawns launcher instances.
              </p>

              <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gar-text-primary mb-3">Event Loop</h4>
              <div class="space-y-2 text-sm text-gar-text-secondary mb-4">
                <div>1. Create IPC server (Unix socket)</div>
                <div>2. Poll for new connections (50ms interval)</div>
                <div>3. Check command channel (non-blocking)</div>
                <div>4. On Show/Toggle: spawn garlaunch process</div>
                <div>5. On Hide: (not yet implemented)</div>
                <div>6. On Status: respond with daemon state</div>
              </div>

              <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gar-text-primary mb-3">Process Spawning</h4>
              <p class="text-gar-text-secondary mb-4">
                When a show/toggle command arrives, daemon spawns a new garlaunch process with appropriate --mode argument. Each launcher instance runs independently.
              </p>

              <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gar-text-primary mb-3">Socket Location</h4>
              <p class="text-gar-text-secondary mb-4">
                $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/garlaunch.sock (fallback: /tmp/garlaunch.sock)
              </p>
            </div>

            <!-- garlaunchctl -->
            <div slot="doc-15">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gar-text-primary mb-4">garlaunchctl</h3>
