              </p>

              <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gar-text-primary mb-3">Commands</h4>
              <div class="space-y-3 mb-4">
                <div class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-gar-bg-secondary/50 border border-gar-text-muted/10">
                  <div class="font-semibold text-gar-text-primary mb-1">show [--mode MODE] [--source PATH]</div>
                  <div class="text-sm text-gar-text-secondary">Show launcher in specified mode</div>
                </div>
                <div class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-gar-bg-secondary/50 border border-gar-text-muted/10">
                  <div class="font-semibold text-gar-text-primary mb-1">hide</div>
                  <div class="text-sm text-gar-text-secondary">Hide launcher (not yet implemented)</div>
                </div>
                <div class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-gar-bg-secondary/50 border border-gar-text-muted/10">
                  <div class="font-semibold text-gar-text-primary mb-1">toggle [--mode MODE]</div>
                  <div class="text-sm text-gar-text-secondary">Toggle launcher visibility</div>
                </div>
                <div class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-gar-bg-secondary/50 border border-gar-text-muted/10">
                  <div class="font-semibold text-gar-text-primary mb-1">status</div>
                  <div class="text-sm text-gar-text-secondary">Query daemon status</div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gar-text-primary mb-3">Fallback Behavior</h4>
              <p class="text-gar-text-secondary mb-4">
                If daemon isn't running (socket not found or connection refused), garlaunchctl spawns garlaunch directly for show/toggle commands. This provides graceful degradation.
              </p>
            </div>

